{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793984317,"nonce":"wTrC8bP4tv187J6KebWLCXcrl70=","title":"Move blinc.rs DNS to Cloudflare so assets.blinc.rs can serve the asset CDN","message":"The docs deploy is blocked on the asset origin (65c14ff322cdabacb7a44b1eea70375263366734e6467bcd675a0df5a38e9743). An R2 custom domain needs blinc.rs to be a zone in the Cloudflare account, and it is not: the account holds only rayde.org.\n\nState, 2026-11-06:\n- Registrar panel at regery.com (registered through Gransy, expires 2027-05-21) has Set Nameservers disabled. Registry status is ACTIVE with no locks, so the block is on the registrar side. The registrar is resending its confirmation email; the owner is waiting on it.\n- Current DNS to carry over: four A (185.199.108.153, .109.153, .110.153, .111.153) and four AAAA (2606:50c0:8000::153 to 8003::153) on the apex for GitHub Pages, one TXT google-site-verification=7vQTsy1k90etWuyVfTZrssv3Whumq1XDDkweOfeDOrk. No MX, no www, no CAA, no DNSSEC.\n- Done meanwhile with wrangler: R2 bucket blinc-assets, CORS for https://blinc.rs and www, r2.dev address enabled as a dev-only interim origin.\n\nSteps once the registrar allows it:\n1. Cloudflare: Add domain blinc.rs on the Free plan, import records, set the apex A/AAAA to DNS only so Pages keeps issuing its certificate.\n2. Registrar: set the two Cloudflare nameservers.\n3. When the zone is Active: wrangler r2 bucket domain add blinc-assets --domain assets.blinc.rs --zone-id \u003cid\u003e, then set repository variable ASSET_BASE_URL to https://assets.blinc.rs and redeploy docs.\n4. Check the site, the Pages certificate and the component gallery still resolve after the nameserver change.\n\nAlso needed for CI, independent of the domain: an R2 S3 access key limited to blinc-assets (dashboard only), set as repository secrets R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID and R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, with R2_ACCOUNT_ID and variable R2_BUCKET.","files":null}]}